;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;\\\" data-mce-fragment=\\\"1\\\"><span style=\\\"border-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;font-family:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-optical-sizing:inherit;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-size:14px;font-stretch:inherit;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-variation-settings:inherit;font-weight:inherit;line-height:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;\\\" data-mce-fragment=\\\"1\\\">Whether it is high-end restaurants with intimate spaces offering personalized menus, hotels featuring bespoke room furnishings to match individual tastes, or specialty coffee shops with unique coffee blends to suit different palates, customization is great at placing the spotlight on the unique aspects of a particular business. It serves as a de facto tool that allows businesses to adjust to market requirements faster and remain with their clients. Eventually, in the HoReCa value chain, engaging on the level of customization isn\\u2019t only a cherry on the cake but goes with a messy vegan doughnut recipe for long-term prosperity and well-being.&nbsp;<\\/span><br><span style=\\\"border-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;font-family:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-optical-sizing:inherit;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-size:14px;font-stretch:inherit;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-variation-settings:inherit;font-weight:inherit;line-height:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;\\\" data-mce-fragment=\\\"1\\\">&nbsp;<\\/span><\\/p><h2 style=\\\"border-width:0px;box-sizing:border-box;color:var(--heading-color);font-family:var(--font-heading-family);font-feature-settings:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-optical-sizing:inherit;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-size:24px;font-stretch:inherit;font-style:inherit;font-variant:inherit;font-variation-settings:inherit;letter-spacing:0px;line-height:1.4;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;\\\" data-